From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:42:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot_jit: dynarmic as the JIT fallback of the AOT code,
 counted, logged and limited

When AOT code (blr, br) reaches an address that is no AOT function, aot_jit.cpp loads the State into a
dynarmic A64 Jit, runs the code found in guest memory, and gives the registers back when it returns to
the x30 the caller left (kept real, so the return addresses JIT code saves on the stack are true). JIT
code that branches to an AOT entry goes back to the AOT code and resumes at x30. Writes to a page the
JIT compiled from (AOT stores, JIT stores, aot_poke) invalidate it, so generated code that changes is
recompiled. Entries, transitions, invalidations and compiled pages are counted; every (target, kind) is
logged; an entry budget, a cycle budget and a nesting depth stop runaway use with an explicit error, as do
no code at an address, an access outside guest memory, an instruction dynarmic cannot translate, an
exception and an svc (Horizon's services are T5). One Jit per host thread, one exclusive monitor.
aot_runtime.h shares the runtime with it; aot_lift.py gets Aot(jit=True, ...) and builds the fixed
objects once per process. 14 tests compare with Unicorn, recompile rewritten code, run an exclusive
counter loop in the JIT on four threads, and check each limit. Skipped without DYNARMIC_DIR.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: T4 of an AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); new JIT fallback and tests, nothing in the host, loader or shader chain changes
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t4-jit-secours)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
